# A/B of two legacy ClusterPolicy builds against the realistic Pod.
#
# 10 requests/s, which looks absurd next to the other presets and is not. With 16
# policy pairs and a 3.8 KB Pod the legacy engine cannot hold 200 requests/s on a
# four-core host: it achieves about 80 and returns roughly a thousand failures,
# several of them 10-second webhook timeouts. Aggregation refuses any run with a
# failed request, correctly, so the rate has to be one the arm can actually serve.
#
# Treat the low rate as a finding about the legacy engine's capacity at this
# shape, not as a handicap applied to it.
ENGINES=${ENGINES:-"baseline kyverno"}
POLICY_COUNT=${POLICY_COUNT:-16}
PAYLOAD_PROFILE=${PAYLOAD_PROFILE:-realistic}
TARGET_RPS=${TARGET_RPS:-10}
TRIALS=${TRIALS:-3}
PROFILE=${PROFILE:-scaling}
